From: nuubOS Project <nuubos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: limit RTL8821CS 5 GHz to 20 MHz

RTL8821CS SDIO devices used on H700 systems can exhibit severe
transmit stalls when operating on 5 GHz with channel widths above
20 MHz.

Testing on the RG35XX Pro shows stable operation on both 2.4 GHz
HT20 and 5 GHz HT20. In contrast, 5 GHz HT40 and VHT80 can produce
multi-second transmit latency and severe packet batching.

Keep 5 GHz support available, but disable HT40 and 80 MHz channel
widths for RTL8821C devices connected over SDIO.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project <nuubos@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
@@ -1707,6 +1707,23 @@
 		sband = rtw_sband_dup(rtwdev, &rtw_band_5ghz);
 		if (!sband)
 			goto err_out;
+
+		/*
+		 * RTL8821CS on H700 systems can exhibit severe TX stalls on
+		 * 5 GHz when operating with channel widths above 20 MHz.
+		 * Keep 5 GHz available while restricting it to 20 MHz.
+		 */
+		if (chip->id == RTW_CHIP_TYPE_8821C &&
+		    rtw_hci_type(rtwdev) == RTW_HCI_TYPE_SDIO) {
+			int i;
+
+			for (i = 0; i < sband->n_channels; i++)
+				sband->channels[i].flags |=
+					IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_80MHZ |
+					IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_HT40PLUS |
+					IEEE80211_CHAN_NO_HT40MINUS;
+		}
+
 		if (chip->ht_supported)
 			rtw_init_ht_cap(rtwdev, &sband->ht_cap);
 		if (chip->vht_supported)
